1. Error and pagination types:
   - ApiError: { code: number, message: string, errors?: Record<string, string[]> }
   - PaginatedResponse<T>: { data: T[], meta: { current_page, total_pages, total_count, per_page } }

2. User/Company types:
   - User: { id, email, name, phone?, company_memberships: CompanyMembership[] }
   - CompanyMembership: { company_id, role }
   - Company: { id, name, settings, custom_fields, created_at, updated_at }

3. Core entity types:
   - Budget: { id, name, amount, remaining_amount, department_id?, archived, active, currency }
   - Department: { id, name, company_id, archived }
   - Supplier: { id, name, email?, phone?, address?, archived }
   - Product: { id, name, description?, sku?, unit_price?, supplier_id? }

4. Transaction types:
   - PurchaseOrder: { id, number, status, supplier_id, line_items: LineItem[], total, created_at, accept_token?, reject_token? }
   - LineItem: { description, quantity, unit_price, budget_id?, tax_rate_id? }
   - Invoice: { id, number, status, supplier_id, purchase_order_id?, amount, created_at }
   - Payment: { id, amount, purchase_order_id?, invoice_id?, created_at }

5. Workflow types:
   - ApprovalFlow: { id, name, steps: ApprovalStep[], conditions?, archived }
   - ApprovalStep: { approver_id, order, condition? }
   - ApprovalCondition: { field, operator, value }

6. Supporting types:
   - TaxRate: { id, name, rate, archived }
   - Webhook: { id, url, events: string[], active }
   - Currency: { code, name, symbol }

All interfaces should use optional properties (?) where fields may not always be present. Export all interfaces for use across the codebase.

